{
  "slug": "lazyline",
  "name": "Lazyline",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Line-level Python profiler skill for Claude Code. Profile any package or script to find exactly which lines are slow, then optimize iteratively.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `lazyline` (Profile Python code with lazyline to find line-level bottlenecks and optimize iteratively).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install lazyline@claude-community` from `TomasVenkrbec/lazyline`.\n\nZero-config, deterministic, line-level Python profiler. Find slow Python code and profile it line by line — no `@profile` decorators, no code changes. Point it at a package or script and get exact hit counts and timing for every line. Subprocesses and multiprocessing pools profiled automatically. Find the lazy lines.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
